    "result_text": "The build passes green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change rejects owner creation when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, responding with 409.\n\n**Implementation** \u2014 a single 3-line guard added to `addOwner` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, reusing the existing `CityCodes.countInCity` helper:\n\n```java\nif (CityCodes.countInCity(owners, owner) >= 50) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n}\n```\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact low:**\n- **One file touched.** `POST /api/owners` (the only create path) is the sole place this rule can live.\n- **Zero new complexity in supporting code.** `CityCodes.countInCity(existing, candidate)` already counts owners sharing a candidate's city (case-insensitively) \u2014 it was previously used only for customer codes. Reusing it means no new helper class or method needed, so no other function's WMC grows.\n- **Minimal edit to `addOwner`.** It sits alongside the existing conflict checks (telephone dup, household dup), reading in the same `owners = findAllOwners()` collection already in scope \u2014 no new data fetch, adding just +1 to the method's cyclomatic complexity.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fill a city to 50, expect the 51st to 409) passes, and the full suite is green.",
